1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,460
Oiran! Oiran!

2
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:06,040
Come on, let's play! Let's play!

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:07,760
Alright then.

4
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:09,040
Oiran!

5
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:12,060
Can you read me a story?

6
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:13,640
Well, certainly.

7
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:15,400
What should I read?

8
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:18,640
Let's see, how about...

9
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:19,260
This one!

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,540
Can you read me this story?

11
00:00:22,140 --> 00:00:24,240
When I finish reading hers, alright?

12
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:26,440
I promise I'll get to yours after.

13
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:29,040
You can just read mine later.

14
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:30,520
Read mine later.

15
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,340
Why are you always copying me?

16
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:35,100
Well, uh...

17
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:36,140
Now, now, you two.

18
00:00:37,480 --> 00:00:39,080
Oh, that reminds me.

19
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:40,880
Come see.

20
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:42,680
I have something to give you two.

21
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:44,840
What is it?

22
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,720
What are you giving us, Oiran?

23
00:00:53,520 --> 00:00:54,660
Oh, wow!

24
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:57,780
But why?

25
00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:01,220
These are really special treasures of yours, aren't they, Oiran?

26
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:02,900
It's alright.

27
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:04,580
Don't you worry about that.

28
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:06,960
You're also very special to me.

29
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:09,020
Which is why I'm giving them to you.

30
00:01:09,020 --> 00:01:10,020
Thank you, Oiran!

31
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:14,120
Thank you, Oiran!

32
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:16,700
Oiran, Oiran!

33
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,160
Put this comb on me!

34
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:19,500
Hurry, hurry!

35
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:21,600
Okay, okay.

36
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:22,720
One at a time.

37
00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:23,600
Oh, though.

38
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:24,180
Oh, you're really special прим.

39
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:26,080
There's still a lot of tears of my needs on Mars in the wrong place.

40
00:01:26,080 --> 00:01:28,760
There's still a lot in Lie.

41
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:58,740
guitar solo

42
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:07,120
See the next clip...

43
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:12,580
...

44
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:15,140
Oh!

45
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:16,480
true

46
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:21,060
uh

47
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:24,700
um

48
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:26,020
um

49
00:02:26,020 --> 00:02:28,660
see

50
00:02:28,660 --> 00:02:33,760
ām

51
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:40,000
yeah

52
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
g

53
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:52,140
Da da da da da da da da da da da da da da do da da da da da da da da da da da da da da da da da da!

54
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:03,380
Nowhere to be found!

55
00:03:03,860 --> 00:03:04,680
That's right!

56
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:07,020
The one with yellow hair?

57
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:08,600
Zenko maybe?

58
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:11,660
She had fainted so we put her to bed to rest.

59
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,160
Now she's not in her room. Should we look for her?

60
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:19,120
Don't bother. I'm sure that the girl is fine.

61
00:03:19,920 --> 00:03:21,760
It's Ashinuke. What do I care?

62
00:03:22,340 --> 00:03:25,660
She left, so it's not our business. Just forget it.

63
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:27,660
What? But Master...

64
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:31,000
Shut the hell up!

65
00:03:33,060 --> 00:03:33,580
Dismissed!

66
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:37,020
Don't ever mention Zenko's name again.

67
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:41,360
Tell the others not to either.

68
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:47,480
This wouldn't have happened if they hadn't got on Oiran Warabihime's nerves.

69
00:03:49,280 --> 00:03:50,760
Both Zenko and Omitsu.

70
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:55,700
I told you!

71
00:03:56,460 --> 00:03:58,720
There's a demon at my house, alright?

72
00:03:59,580 --> 00:04:00,100
Really?

73
00:04:00,820 --> 00:04:02,960
I'm telling you, it looked like this!

74
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:04,840
You know what I mean, like this!

75
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:07,620
Yeah, I totally believe you.

76
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:09,740
Just hold on a second.

77
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:11,320
Like this!

78
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:13,200
Now you see what I'm saying?

79
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:18,060
Yeah, anyway, Mr. Uzui and Zenitsu should be coming to check in soon.

80
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:19,460
And it was like this!

81
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,620
I couldn't be any clearer here if I tried!

82
00:04:21,880 --> 00:04:22,740
Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

83
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:24,800
Zenitsu won't be coming.

84
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:29,400
There's no doubt.

85
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,340
This guy's the real deal.

86
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,080
He didn't make a sound.

87
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:35,600
Not even the slightest puff of air.

88
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:38,680
Wait, Zenitsu's not coming?

89
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:40,320
What do you mean by that?

90
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:44,740
I feel bad now about putting you all through this.

91
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:52,400
It seems I was so desperate to rescue my wives in time that I made some poor decisions regarding the mission.

92
00:04:52,400 --> 00:04:56,500
As it stands, Zenitsu is missing.

93
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,780
There's been no contact since last night.

94
00:04:58,780 --> 00:05:01,600
You two should leave now.

95
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,440
Now you're ranked too low for this.

96
00:05:04,440 --> 00:05:07,980
If the demon here turns out to be an upper rank, you'll be dead weight.

97
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:12,840
If you vanish from here, they'll just assume that you're dead.

98
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:19,800
Therefore, I'm continuing on my own.

99
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:21,180
Please, Mr. Uzui.

100
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,400
We can help-

101
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:23,220
Don't be ashamed.

102
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:26,080
Life is all about survival.

103
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,980
So take this chance and get out.

104
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:31,900
Get back here, old man!

105
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:38,460
Maybe he's not able to put his trust in us.

106
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,820
Is it because we're the lowest rank?

107
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,800
We're not the lowest rank now.

108
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:44,660
We're Kanaway.

109
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:46,100
We did get promoted.

110
00:05:46,540 --> 00:05:46,740
Huh?

111
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:49,000
Did you forget the rankings?

112
00:05:49,980 --> 00:05:52,860
We used to be Mizunoto at the very bottom, right?

113
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,940
Well, now we're fourth from the bottom.

114
00:05:55,200 --> 00:05:55,680
Kanaway!

115
00:05:56,080 --> 00:05:56,800
Wait, what?

116
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:58,320
You guys actually caught up to me?

117
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:00,920
Eat it, you piss-head!

118
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:01,540
Crybaby!

119
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:03,700
We'll be moving past you in no time!

120
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:05,640
Say that again, you stupid bore!

121
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:07,260
I'll do you one better!

122
00:06:11,200 --> 00:06:12,160
You ready?

123
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:13,240
Watch this.

124
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,500
Show me my current ranking.

125
00:06:20,940 --> 00:06:21,880
Cool, huh?

126
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:25,760
What was that?

127
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,320
What?

128
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:31,120
They messed with your hand on Wisteria Mountain, right?

129
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:34,260
I think I remember that, but I'm not sure.

130
00:06:34,460 --> 00:06:35,480
I was so exhausted.

131
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:37,980
Wisteria Flower Engraving.

132
00:06:38,160 --> 00:06:41,100
You have to say that phrase and flex your muscles to invoke it.

133
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:44,240
I had no clue we could do stuff like that.

134
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:46,580
It proves we're Demonslayer Core.

135
00:06:48,580 --> 00:06:50,180
Come on now, cheer up!

136
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:52,160
That's right!

137
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:53,800
We don't have time to mope around!

138
00:06:54,340 --> 00:06:57,120
I'll head over to your Okimoto house once night falls.

139
00:06:57,840 --> 00:06:59,060
So wait for me till then.

140
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:01,260
It's too risky to make a move on your own.

141
00:07:01,260 --> 00:07:03,120
Why should I wait for you?

142
00:07:03,220 --> 00:07:05,920
I still need to finish investigating my own house.

143
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:11,020
I already told you the Demons had my house, so quit wasting our time!

144
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:12,180
Wait till night!

145
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:13,440
How stupid are you?

146
00:07:13,980 --> 00:07:15,420
Do they ever shut up?

147
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:17,400
That's not what I meant!

148
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:24,020
Mr. Uzui was patrolling outside of our houses during the night, right?

149
00:07:24,740 --> 00:07:25,700
Ow, ow, ow!

150
00:07:25,940 --> 00:07:31,460
Even so, Zenitsu still disappeared, and the demon over at your place is nowhere to be seen right now!

151
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:35,740
Minosuke, can you please stop smacking me around?

152
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:39,760
Which leads me to believe there's a passage that leads into the building!

153
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:41,720
Passage?

154
00:07:41,720 --> 00:07:50,300
That's right, and it hasn't been spotted going in and out of the house, which means the demon is probably working from the inside.

155
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:58,440
If that is what's happening here, and it's cleverly disguising itself as a human, then it would kill its victims carefully.

156
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,540
Makes sense, right?

157
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:02,480
Yeah, it does.

158
00:08:03,420 --> 00:08:05,800
Cleaning up after a murder would be a real hassle.

159
00:08:06,720 --> 00:08:08,720
Washing bloodstains is no easy task.

160
00:08:09,520 --> 00:08:11,120
This is a nightlife district.

161
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:15,420
Which can be convenient for demons, but also an obstacle.

162
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:18,180
They've gotta work at night, after all.

163
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:20,560
It'd be odd if they weren't around.

164
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,280
You're right.

165
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:30,020
I think Zenitsu and Mr. Uzui's wives are all still alive, so I'll proceed with that in mind.

166
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:31,880
And I will rescue them.

167
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:36,020
I want you to take action with that in mind too, Inosuke.

168
00:08:36,020 --> 00:08:40,220
But at the same time, I don't want you to die.

169
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:42,960
Is that all right with you?

170
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:53,680
I think everything you said just now is exactly what I was about to say myself.

171
00:08:53,680 --> 00:09:00,640
Oiran, we brought you your tea.

172
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:02,720
Why, thank you.

173
00:09:03,140 --> 00:09:04,660
I can do the rest of it myself.

174
00:09:05,080 --> 00:09:06,200
You two go on and have dinner.

175
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:07,480
All right.

176
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:12,540
We'll be going on ahead then.

177
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:13,600
Don't be long.

178
00:09:15,940 --> 00:09:16,660
Huh?

179
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:19,400
I love you, Oiran Koinatsu.

180
00:09:19,920 --> 00:09:21,180
I love you too, Oiran.

181
00:09:23,860 --> 00:09:24,900
How sweet.

182
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:26,600
I love you both as well.

183
00:09:26,980 --> 00:09:28,660
Now get to dinner, you two.

184
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:29,980
Okay.

185
00:09:29,980 --> 00:09:33,880
Oiran looked happy, didn't she?

186
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:35,200
She did.

187
00:09:40,120 --> 00:09:41,920
Those girls are something else.

188
00:09:46,440 --> 00:09:47,400
Miss Koinatsu?

189
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:52,180
Osumi, it's you.

190
00:09:52,180 --> 00:09:54,740
Forgive me for intruding just now.

191
00:09:55,540 --> 00:09:57,440
However, I have a favor to ask.

192
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:00,440
I'm leaving the Tokito house after this.

193
00:10:00,960 --> 00:10:02,740
Would you give Master my payment for lodging?

194
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:08,780
What's going on?

195
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:11,420
And why are you dressed so...

196
00:10:11,420 --> 00:10:13,900
I had to dress as a woman for my mission.

197
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:15,580
But I'm actually a guy.

198
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:18,580
Oh, I already knew that.

199
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:20,020
Your voice gave it away.

200
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:21,220
Sorry.

201
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:24,020
What?

202
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:27,440
Well, it was obvious from the start.

203
00:10:27,740 --> 00:10:29,000
I've known the whole time.

204
00:10:29,580 --> 00:10:31,440
I admit I was a bit curious

205
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:33,040
as to what you were up to.

206
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:38,320
I guess I was busted from the beginning.

207
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,840
But you have your reasons, right?

208
00:10:42,540 --> 00:10:44,420
Were you worried about Suma for real?

209
00:10:44,420 --> 00:10:45,500
Or was that a lie?

210
00:10:46,060 --> 00:10:46,480
No!

211
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:47,840
I was telling the truth!

212
00:10:48,340 --> 00:10:49,640
I would never lie like that!

213
00:10:50,520 --> 00:10:51,720
As for everyone that vanished,

214
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:53,560
I promise I'll rescue them.

215
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:56,260
Why, thank you.

216
00:10:56,860 --> 00:10:58,380
I think I needed to hear that.

217
00:10:59,860 --> 00:11:00,760
Because you see,

218
00:11:01,180 --> 00:11:03,760
I'm actually leaving this district for good tomorrow.

219
00:11:04,420 --> 00:11:05,800
No way, are you really?

220
00:11:06,140 --> 00:11:07,760
You must be ecstatic about that.

221
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:09,820
It seems there's someone

222
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:11,700
who would want even me as his wife.

223
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:14,260
Which makes me so happy.

224
00:11:14,260 --> 00:11:20,900
But that could be why I've been worried sick lately

225
00:11:20,900 --> 00:11:22,560
about those I'm leaving behind.

226
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:25,520
Even if I thought I knew something was wrong,

227
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:29,260
I'd have no way of even looking into it.

228
00:11:30,620 --> 00:11:31,980
But that isn't your fault.

229
00:11:32,780 --> 00:11:34,100
Please, don't worry about it.

230
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:35,960
All you can do is move forward.

231
00:11:35,960 --> 00:11:38,360
And you too.

232
00:11:38,360 --> 00:11:40,900
I don't want you to disappear either, Sumi.

233
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:42,420
Be careful.

234
00:11:42,420 --> 00:11:54,640
Now then, I'll be off.

235
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,060
I wish you the best.

236
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:01,960
Thank you, Sumi.

237
00:12:02,480 --> 00:12:03,660
Best of luck to you.

238
00:12:04,340 --> 00:12:05,620
And I'm counting on you

239
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:06,700
to save Suma.

240
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:07,980
Right.

241
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:27,260
Oh, did you forget something?

242
00:12:27,260 --> 00:12:31,020
No, but thank you.

243
00:12:31,320 --> 00:12:33,120
However, I really should devour you

244
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,480
before I do forget.

245
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:38,180
Since tonight happens to be

246
00:12:38,180 --> 00:12:39,360
your last night here,

247
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:41,600
you can't leave without saying goodbye.

248
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:52,240
Not good.

249
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:54,020
The sun's almost done setting.

250
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:57,280
I've got to get to Inosuke's place fast.

251
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,100
There's a scent.

252
00:13:04,680 --> 00:13:06,440
It's faint, but it smells sweet.

253
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:08,960
It's a demon.

254
00:13:09,620 --> 00:13:10,440
It has to be.

255
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:11,780
And it's nearby.

256
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:13,280
This is bad.

257
00:13:25,760 --> 00:13:26,700
He's late.

258
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:28,280
It's almost nightfall

259
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:29,700
and he's still not here yet.

260
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:31,120
Way to mess things up,

261
00:13:31,200 --> 00:13:31,760
Soichiro.

262
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:34,760
I'll just take action by myself.

263
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:36,280
The spirit of coming through

264
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:37,760
flowing within my heart.

265
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:43,120
Come on out, mice!

266
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:44,500
And bring my swords!

267
00:13:49,260 --> 00:13:50,120
Oh, man.

268
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:52,300
Uzu is something else, huh?

269
00:13:52,900 --> 00:13:53,420
Muscle.

270
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:54,480
Muscle.

271
00:13:55,340 --> 00:13:55,860
Muscle!

272
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:57,840
I gotta thank him

273
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:58,560
for setting me up

274
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:00,140
with these muscular mice of his.

275
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,120
I wanna boss around

276
00:14:02,120 --> 00:14:03,380
some ninjoo, too!

277
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:04,720
